<http://data.silknow.org/event/8fe18716-6731-378a-9e4a-f6ad8ab3bb32>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Transferred from India Museum 1879. Textile was cut into fragments from a garment for use by John Forbes Watson in Second Series of 'Textile Manufactures of India, c.1873, v.401-458 'Kincobs', No.431: 'KINCOB / Width, 30 1/2 Ins. / AHMEDABAD / No.431, SECOND SERIES / \"11626\"'. Slip book entry 11626: 'Kinkaub Coat [and] Trowsers [only] Jacket & Skirt / oodypore / 55 / Kinkaub probably made in Ahmedabad / Ungurka & Coat Taken out for Second Series of F-Book'."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6d74c149-a5c4-3ee8-8752-3fee9c7517e7> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Transferred from India Museum 1879. Textile was cut into fragments from a garment for use by John Forbes Watson in Second Series of 'Textile Manufactures of India, c.1873, v.401-458 'Kincobs', No.431: 'KINCOB / Width, 30 1/2 Ins. / AHMEDABAD / No.431, SECOND SERIES / \"11626\"'. Slip book entry 11626: 'Kinkaub Coat [and] Trowsers [only] Jacket & Skirt / oodypore / 55 / Kinkaub probably made in Ahmedabad / Ungurka & Coat Taken out for Second Series of F-Book'."@en .

